From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Contributor <me@Contributorr.co>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_fg: report current_now with ABI sign

The qcom_fg gen3 (pmi8998) fuel gauge on the AYN Odin reports
POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW as negative while charging and positive
while discharging. That is the opposite of the Linux power-supply ABI,
which defines current_now as positive when charging and negative when
discharging.

UPower's up-device-supply-battery.c has a quirk (added for axp20x-style
batteries) that, regardless of POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS, forces the device
state to DISCHARGING whenever current_now < 0 and the battery is not
full:

	values.state = up_device_supply_get_state (native);
	if (values.state != UP_DEVICE_STATE_FULLY_CHARGED &&
	    get_sysfs_attr_uncached (native, "current_now") < 0.0)
		values.state = UP_DEVICE_STATE_DISCHARGING;

Because the FG reports a negative current_now while charging, UPower
reports the battery as "discharging" even though status=Charging and the
pmi8998-charger line-power supply is online. Steam / gamescope read the
UPower state, so the battery indicator never shows the charging bolt
while plugged in.

Flip the reported sign at the property boundary so it matches the ABI.
The internal current-sign fallback in the status property and consumers
that use magnitude only (mangohud uses fabs()) are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Contributor <me@Contributorr.co>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
index 9c3f0aa..8b1d2e5 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -983,5 +983,18 @@ static int qcom_fg_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW:
 		ret = chip->ops->get_current(chip, &val->intval);
+		/*
+		 * The Linux power-supply ABI defines current_now as positive
+		 * while charging and negative while discharging. This FG
+		 * reports the opposite sign, which makes UPower
+		 * (up-device-supply-battery.c) override status=Charging and
+		 * report the battery as "discharging" whenever
+		 * current_now < 0 -- so the Steam/gamescope battery icon never
+		 * shows the charging state. Flip the sign to match the ABI.
+		 * The internal status fallback reads get_current() directly and
+		 * magnitude-only consumers (mangohud) use fabs(), so neither is
+		 * affected by this.
+		 */
+		val->intval = -val->intval;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW:
 		ret = chip->ops->get_voltage(chip, &val->intval);
--
